  "narrative": "I assessed all newly delivered discovery results under the signed convention: for direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a more negative raw CRISPR dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means a less negative raw score, i.e. weaker dependency. All due results had valid Welch comparisons with both cells containing at least 20 observations.\n\nThe MDM2/CDKN2A association remains robust. H213 tests CDKN2A loss in a broad low-9p21 stratum, copy_number_9p21 <= -0.25; R182 is +0.129 (0.091 to 0.167), far above the approximate MDM2 clinical effect scale of about 0.025-0.027. This supports the dataset-specific association without depending on the stricter 9p21 cutpoint or exact MTAP/TP53 splits. H214 tests high Cas9 activity, cas9_activity_pct >= 80; R183 is +0.147 (0.092 to 0.202), again clinically meaningful and consistent with a screening-quality-robust association. I therefore accept and close both exact claims.\n\nThe core dependency associations are also robust in high-serum and low-ploidy contexts. H215, R184, gives +0.784 for MSI-high versus non-MSI-high WRN dependency in 10% serum; H221, R190, gives +0.813 in low ploidy <=2.5. H216, R185, gives +0.800 for TP53-loss versus TP53-intact USP7 dependency in 10% serum, interpreted as weaker USP7 dependency with TP53 loss under direction +1; H218, R187, gives +0.820 in low ploidy. H217, R186, gives +0.814 for KEAP1-loss versus KEAP1-intact NFE2L2 dependency in 10% serum, interpreted as weaker NFE2L2 dependency with KEAP1 loss under direction +1; H219, R188, gives +0.791 in low ploidy. H220, R189, gives +0.791 for SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA4-intact SMARCA2 dependency in low ploidy. These are enormous effects relative to the 10% clinical scale and are concordant with previously accepted core associations. They reduce concern that the original effects are confined to high-ploidy, non-Avana, low-quality, or serum-limited screens. I accept and close these exact robustness claims.\n\nThe expression-conditioned MYC hypotheses are not supported. H222 tests whether MYC amplification has a clinically meaningful stronger-DHX9 association only when RNaseq MYC expression is high; R191 is -0.016 (-0.048 to +0.017). The interval includes no effect and its upper bound remains below the approximate clinical scale. H223 similarly gives -0.008 (-0.039 to +0.024) for RPL11. Thus restricting to high-MYC expression does not establish the expected MYC-amplification-specific dependency effects; I reject and close both.\n\nH224, EGFR amplification versus KRAS dependency in KRAS-wild-type adenocarcinoma, remains borderline and unresolved. R193 is +0.014 (-0.023 to +0.050). The point estimate is below the approximate clinical scale, but the interval includes clinically meaningful stronger KRAS dependency. I therefore do not accept it as clinically meaningful, but I also cannot reject it without further evidence. It remains active for adequately powered discovery follow-up.\n\nFrom a critical-reviewer standpoint, these analyses are associations among measured variables in the supplied panel, not causal claims or claims of external generalizability. The strongest accepted findings are supported by very large signed effects and multiple internal strata; the borderline MYC and EGFR results are not promoted because their uncertainty and effect estimates are too small. No validation request is made because the new voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 appraise update. Signed convention retained. New accepted and closed dataset-specific robustness/association results: CDKN2A loss remains strongly associated with stronger MDM2 dependency in broad low-9p21 <= -0.25 (H213) and high Cas9 >=80 (H214). MSI-high remains strongly associated with stronger WRN dependency in 10% serum (H215) and low ploidy <=2.5 (H221). TP53 loss remains associated with weaker USP7 dependency in 10% serum (H216) and low ploidy <=2.5 (H218). KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency in 10% serum (H217) and low ploidy <=2.5 (H219). SMARCA4 loss remains associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency in low ploidy <=2.5 (H220). MYC amplification in high-MYC-expression contexts does not support stronger DHX9 or RPL11 dependency (H222, H223 rejected). EGFR amplification in KRAS-wild-type adenocarcinoma versus KRAS dependency remains unresolved active (H224), point estimate small but interval includes clinically meaningful values. Validation budget is exhausted.\n\nCore accepted associations remain: MSI-high stronger WRN; SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2; TP53 loss weaker USP7; KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2; CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2. These are supported in multiple independent strata and by earlier validation. The exact TP53-loss MTAP-intact MDM2 claim H158 remains downgraded/unresolved after failed validation, but broader CDKN2A-MDM2 evidence is not overturned. Future analyses should focus on populated strata and avoid sparse exact MDM2 co-deletion splits: H209/H210 for TP53-loss low-9p21, H211 for MTAP loss in CDKN2A-intact broad low-9p21, H212 for refined EGFR amp in TP53-intact KRAS/BRAF/ERBB2-wild-type adenocarcinoma, and robustness tests for EGFR/other borderline candidates."
}

