  "narrative": "No independent validation deadlines were listed and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted. I therefore completed a synthesis assessment of the existing independent validation evidence and finalized the supported conclusions. The signed convention remains: for direction -1 claims a positive estimate means the exposed group has a more negative raw dependency score, i.e. stronger dependency; for direction +1 claims a positive estimate means a less negative raw score, i.e. weaker dependency.\n\nSUPPORTED CORE DATASET-SPECIFIC ASSOCIATIONS. Five associations are supported by large discovery effects and independent internal validation, and each is many-fold above the approximate 10 percent clinical effect scale. First, MSI-high lineages show much stronger WRN dependency: H6 R6 +0.790, 95 percent discovery interval +0.760 to +0.819; validation R53 +0.821, interval +0.766 to +0.877. Second, SMARCA4 loss shows much stronger SMARCA2 dependency: H7 R7 +0.784, +0.765 to +0.803; validation R39 +0.801, +0.771 to +0.830. Third, TP53 loss is associated with much weaker USP7 dependency under direction +1: H11 R11 +0.802, +0.782 to +0.822; validation R13 +0.800, +0.769 to +0.832. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with much weaker NFE2L2 dependency under direction +1: H17 signed R8 +0.796, +0.776 to +0.816; validation R26 +0.791, +0.761 to +0.821. Fifth, CDKN2A loss is associated with stronger MDM2 dependency: H80 R59 +0.117, +0.082 to +0.152; validation R66 +0.130, +0.078 to +0.182. The CDKN2A-MDM2 effect is smaller than the four core effects but still several-fold above the clinical threshold and is robust in many independent strata.\n\nROBUSTNESS. The core associations remain concordant in library, screen-quality, batch, ploidy, serum, matched-QC, and co-mutation strata. The accepted exact strata for CDKN2A-MDM2 include TP53-intact and TP53-loss broad contexts, low-9p21 contexts, MTAP-intact broad contexts, and low-9p21 MTAP-intact contexts. Several of these were validated: H83, H141, H153, and H80. Some exact MTAP-loss strata are less stable at validation: H85 validation R92 has point +0.096 but lower -0.002, and H132 validation R118 has point +0.108 with lower -0.024. I retained them as accepted because the discovery intervals are strong and clinically meaningful, but they should not be presented as the primary CDKN2A-MDM2 evidence. The broader CDKN2A-MDM2 conclusion does not depend on these exact MTAP-loss or exact triple-context cells.\n\nUNRESOLVED EXACT MDM2/MTAP CONTEXTS. H158, CDKN2A loss in TP53-loss MTAP-intact tumors, was clinically meaningful in discovery R134 +0.0998, +0.018 to +0.181, but independent validation R157 was smaller and imprecise +0.059, -0.071 to +0.189. I keep H158 unresolved and active. H99, MTAP loss among CDKN2A-loss tumors, remains active unresolved with discovery R84 +0.064, -0.025 to +0.153. These exact contexts need adequately powered broad strata such as active H209, H210, and H211 rather than sparse triple splits.\n\nNEGATIVE FINDINGS. Several intuitive biomarker-dependency hypotheses are rejected in this panel because intervals are near zero and point estimates are below the clinical threshold. KRAS mutation is not a clinically meaningful predictor of KRAS dependency: H1 R1 +0.014, -0.004 to +0.031. BRAF V600E is not clinically meaningful for BRAF dependency: H2 R2 -0.017, -0.045 to +0.012. ERBB2 amplification is not clinically meaningful for ERBB2 dependency: H4 R4 +0.0015. MYC amplification is not clinically meaningful for DHX9, RPL11, POLR2A, or KIF18A, including a high-MYC-expression stratum: H222 R191 -0.016, -0.048 to +0.017 and H223 R192 -0.008, -0.039 to +0.024. RB1 loss is not clinically meaningful for KIF18A: H95 R75 +0.008. BRCA2 loss is null for KIF18A and WRN: H20 R25 and H205 R180. NF1 loss is null for RIT1, KRAS, and STAT3: H72 R64, H73 R65, H96 R76. PIK3CA mutation is null for STAT3: H12 R12. STK11 loss is null for KRAS dependency and SMARCA2: H54 R38 and H138 R117. MTAP loss is not established as a generic MDM2 driver: H81 R98, H94 R74, and H178 R170 are rejected, while H99 and H158 remain unresolved. Research markers D, E, and F are broadly null across the major dependencies; validated example is H42 R60 -0.008 and R79 -0.001 for USP7.\n\nBORDERLINE UNRESOLVED SIGNALS. EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency remains borderline unresolved. H3 R3 +0.025, -0.000 to +0.050 is near but not sufficiently above the clinical threshold; adenocarcinoma and driver-wild-type strata H71 R52 +0.021, -0.017 to +0.059 and H208 R181 +0.021, -0.011 to +0.054 remain similar. H224, EGFR amplification versus KRAS dependency in KRAS-wild-type adenocarcinoma, is also borderline: R193 +0.014, -0.023 to +0.050. ERBB2 amplification versus STAT3 H175 R156 +0.022, -0.015 to +0.059 is borderline active. These are not promoted to accepted claims.\n\nNEXT ANALYSES. The most informative next analyses are discovery comparisons that avoid sparse cells and address the two main open uncertainties. First, run active H209, H210, and H211 to separate CDKN2A-specific MDM2 effects from broader 9p21 or MTAP context using broad low-9p21 strata. Second, run H212 and the newly proposed interaction of EGFR amplification by KRAS-mutant status on EGFR dependency to determine whether the borderline EGFR signal is concentrated in KRAS-wild-type adenocarcinoma; also run H224 and active EGFR/STAT3/other unresolved predictors if cells allow. Third, complete active core robustness claims where power is adequate, including batch, KY-library, and matched-QC strata, but no new validation can be requested because the validation budget is exhausted.\n\nGENERALIZABILITY AND CAUSALITY. All accepted statements are associations among measured variables in the supplied panel, supported by internal validation. They are not proof that the measured alteration causes the dependency, and they are not external clinical generalizability claims. In particular, the large WRN and SMARCA2 effects are strong evidence of context-specific dependency patterns, but causal mechanism requires direct perturbation or independent experimental replication.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 synthesis final-state update. Signed convention retained: direction -1 positive means stronger exposed dependency; direction +1 positive means weaker exposed dependency. Core accepted validated associations remain H6 MSI-high stronger WRN R6+R53; H7 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 R7+R39; H11 TP53 loss weaker USP7 R11+R13; H17 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 R8+R26; H80 CDKN2A loss stronger MDM2 R59+R66. These are many-fold above the approximate 10 percent clinical effect scale. CDKN2A-MDM2 is robust across many strata and multiple validations, but exact MTAP-loss and exact TP53-loss/MTAP-intact strata are less stable: H85 and H132 retained as accepted with validation precision caveats, H158 downgraded unresolved active after validation R157, H99 remains unresolved active. Broad low-9p21 H209/H210/H211 are the most informative next MDM2 analyses. Negative findings include KRAS, BRAF, ERBB2, MYC amplification, RB1, BRCA2, NF1, PIK3CA, STK11, and research marker nulls. EGFR amplification versus EGFR dependency remains borderline unresolved H3/H71/H208; H224 EGFR amp versus KRAS dependency is borderline active. New proposal added: interaction of EGFR amplification by KRAS-mutant status on dependency_EGFR, plus media-stratum interactions for core WRN/USP7/NFE2L2 robustness. No validation budget remains. Final conclusions are dataset-specific associations, not causal or external generalizability claims."
}

