  "narrative": "No assessments are due and independent validation is exhausted, so this exploration is deliberately discovery-only and focused on adequately powered broad robustness checks for the five accepted core dataset-specific associations. I retain the signed convention from the ledger: for direction -1 claims, a positive reported estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1 claims, a positive reported estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group. The accepted core effects are MSI-high/stronger WRN (H6/R6/R53), SMARCA4 loss/stronger SMARCA2 (H7/R7/R39), TP53 loss/weaker USP7 (H11/R11/R13), KEAP1 loss/weaker NFE2L2 after direction correction (H17/R8/R26), and CDKN2A loss/stronger MDM2 (H80/R59/R66). For the four near-0.8 core effects, robust stratum evidence should remain far above the practical 0.1 benchmark; for CDKN2A-MDM2 the expected robust magnitude is around the 0.1-0.15 range and should be interpreted as locus-associated, not exact CDKN2A-only mechanism.\n\nThe new proposals test whether these accepted associations persist in three broad, measured, adequately powered contexts: media_serum_pct = 5%, age_category = adult, and cas9_activity_pct >= 80%. Media serum is a meaningful culture-condition predictor that could alter dependency scoring through growth stress or selection pressure. Adult age category probes population/context robustness beyond already-tested QC, mutational, ploidy, library, batch, KRAS, TP53, MTAP, and adherent-growth strata. High Cas9 activity is a technical-quality predictor; high-activity screens should show the true biological associations most cleanly, so attenuated or null findings there would be more concerning than attenuation in low-quality screens. I propose all five core associations at media 5%; adult strata for SMARCA2, USP7, NFE2L2, and MDM2, since WRN already has an accepted adult stratum (H275/R239); and high-Cas9 strata for SMARCA2, USP7, and NFE2L2, since WRN and MDM2 already have accepted cas9_activity_pct >= 80 strata (H65/R44 and H214/R183).\n\nI deliberately do not propose additional direct EGFR, ERBB2, KRAS, BRAF, MYC, NF1, BRCA2, PIK3CA, STK11, or research-marker D/E/F comparisons. The ledger has repeatedly shown these direct marker matches are small and not scientifically meaningful on the observed dependency scale, and further splits would mainly add multiple-testing noise. I also avoid sparse exact co-deletion cells because prior narrow CDKN2A/MTAP/9p21/TP53 splits produced unstable or underpowered results. These proposals are falsifiable robustness tests for associations in this supplied lung cell-line dataset; a positive robust result supports context-specific reproducibility, while a null stratum would indicate that the original association is not universal in that context, is confounded by the stratum, or is too small to survive subset filtering. None of these analyses establish causal dependency mechanisms or external clinical generalizability.",
