{
  "narrative": "No assessments are due and no new validation was released at this synthesis; the independent validation budget is exhausted and the existing validation evidence is already represented in the ledger. I therefore finalize the inference from the supplied lung adenocarcinoma CRISPR dataset without reopening negative clusters. All estimates are read as signed to the registered hypothesis direction: for direction -1, a positive signed estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive signed estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group. I use approximately 0.10 CRISPR-score units as the practical scale implied by the task, while treating the very large ~0.8-unit associations as decisive and the ~0.1-unit CDKN2A-MDM2 association as moderate and locus-entangled. Supported findings are strongest for four dataset-specific associations. First, MSI-high is associated with stronger WRN dependency: discovery R6 +0.790 95% CI 0.760 to 0.819, independent validation R53 +0.821 95% CI 0.766 to 0.877, with concordant robustness across sex, ploidy, library, batch, Cas9, growth, media, ROC-AUC, mutation burden, KRAS, TP53, and other broad strata. Second, SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency: discovery R7 +0.784 95% CI 0.765 to 0.803, validation R39 +0.801 95% CI 0.771 to 0.830; ARID1A co-loss does not materially modify the core SMARCA4 association, H236 R205 +0.037 95% CI -0.015 to 0.089. Third, TP53 loss is associated with weaker USP7 dependency: discovery R11 +0.802 95% CI 0.782 to 0.822, validation R13 +0.800 95% CI 0.769 to 0.832; this persists across many technical and genomic contexts. Fourth, KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; the original stronger-dependency direction H8 was rejected and the reversed H17 was accepted with signed R8 +0.796 95% CI 0.776 to 0.816 and validation R26 +0.791 95% CI 0.761 to 0.821. Fifth, CDKN2A loss is associated with a moderate increase in MDM2 dependency: overall discovery R59 +0.117 95% CI 0.082 to 0.152, validation R66 +0.130 95% CI 0.078 to 0.182, with multiple concordant strata, especially 9p21 deletion contexts such as H141 R121 +0.122 and validation R131 +0.111 and H153 R132 +0.113 and validation R144 +0.152. The safest interpretation is a broad CDKN2A-loss or 9p21 locus association rather than an independently validated narrow subgroup effect or a pure CDKN2A-only mechanism; MTAP, TP53-loss, and intermediate-Cas9 co-alteration strata are near the practical benchmark or have validation intervals crossing zero, including H85 R92 +0.096 CI -0.002 to 0.195, H132 R118 +0.108 CI -0.024 to 0.239, H158 R157 +0.059 CI -0.071 to 0.188, and H311 R276 +0.025 CI -0.062 to 0.113. Negative findings: direct marker-to-marker dependency hypotheses are generally not supported at a meaningful scale. KRAS mutation is null for KRAS dependency, R1 +0.014 CI -0.004 to 0.031; BRAF V600E is small and opposite, R2 -0.017 CI -0.045 to 0.012; EGFR amplification is small even in EGFR-oriented contexts, R3 +0.025 CI -0.000 to 0.051, with strata not confirming; ERBB2 amplification is null for ERBB2 dependency, R4 +0.001 CI -0.027 to 0.030; TP53 loss is not meaningful for MDM2 dependency, R5 +0.009 CI -0.016 to 0.034. MYC amplification is null or subthreshold for DHX9, RPL11, POLR2A, KIF18A, STAT3, and USP7, including MYC-expression contexts; NF1 loss is null for RIT1, KRAS, and STAT3; BRCA2 loss is null for KIF18A and WRN; PIK3CA mutation is null for STAT3 and other marker outcomes; STK11 loss is null for KRAS and SMARCA2; RB1-loss reverse SMARCA2 exploration H242 R204 +0.048 CI -0.003 to 0.099 is not meaningful. Synthetic research markers D, E, and F are broadly null, including validated USP7/research marker E, H42 R60 -0.008 CI -0.040 to 0.025 and R79 -0.001 CI -0.049 to 0.046. Interaction tests for lineage subtype, media serum, TP53, KEAP1, SMARCA4/ARID1A, and most MDM2 co-deletion dissections are near zero, underpowered, or not practically meaningful. Unresolved uncertainty: the female-stratum tests H313-H316 remain active and should complete sex robustness for SMARCA2, USP7, NFE2L2, and MDM2; H43 is invalid due insufficient cells; H311 is closed unresolved because the intermediate Cas9 MDM2 estimate is small and imprecise; several narrow CDKN2A/MTAP/9p21 subgroup claims remain mechanistically unresolved because validation intervals cross zero or include subthreshold effects. These statements are associations within the supplied dataset, not causal dependency mechanisms, biomarker utility, or external clinical generalizability claims. The most informative next analysis is independent external orthogonal replication of the five core associations. If further internal analysis is possible, finish H313-H316 and replace sparse binary co-deletion cuts with a continuous 9p21 copy-number and CDKN2A/MTAP dosage model for MDM2 dependency; otherwise do not reopen the direct KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, MYC, NF1, BRCA2, PIK3CA, STK11, RB1, APC, SMAD4, or research-marker clusters without substantially larger external evidence.",
